{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789798122,"nonce":"KLajdZzTiehp9koXTSIRNLeaKCQ=","title":"LLVM: a runtime symbol call with no registered signature returned i32 0","message":"`compile_call` shaped a `HirCallable::Symbol` call by the registered ZRTL\nsignature and, with none registered, declared the callee void and used\n`i32 0` as its result. `zyntax_box_get_opaque`, which the SSA builder\nemits to read a struct out of a dynamic value, has no registered\nsignature, so the header pointer it returns was an `i32 0` and the next\nGEP through it panicked (`into_pointer_value`), losing every LLVM\npromotion of a function that unboxes a list, dict or set: nqueens'\n`place` once its calls were few enough for the tier.\n\nFix: with no signature, the call's declared HIR result type shapes the\nreturn, an address for an aggregate held by reference. A GEP whose base\nis not an address is now a codegen error naming the value, not a panic.","files":null}]}